WEBVTT

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.480
The story until now.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:16.050
Infected with the mysterious disease “ochappy”, Nozomu is rushed to a sanatorium atop a hill.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:21.460
Because of that, a large number of phone novel readers who feel the need to pity something flock in chanting

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.000
“How pitiful, how pitiful!”

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.550
In this atmosphere where they'll be disappointed if he doesn't die,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.110
he learns from a doctor the true name of his disease: “aeromonas”.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:40.510
He worries daily that everyone associates this disease with a hot date with Mona and he worries daily,

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.830
but in reality it's a fish disease so there's something not quite right there.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.410
Now he's inconvenienced.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.310
The audience which expects him to die has come again.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.870
In the end, among them is a former Giocatore on a journey to find himself.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:58.430
Bringing along TV cameras, he hoists a soccer ball with “Dream” written on the side.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.300
A measles epidemic, huh.

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.550
You'd better get yourself vaccinated.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:56.290
Miyo (age 5) over in 3-chome seems to have the measles.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.680
You should go spend the night there and get infected.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.030
Why do I have to go and get myself infected on purpose!?

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.520
It's pretty nasty when you get them as an adult,

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.750
so they said “Go get measles when you're a kid” in the old days.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:12.540
But nowadays, you need to do it the right way and go get your shots.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.530
Medically, that's correct, but...

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:17.210
Teacher?

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.740
Not just Majiru.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:23.250
Don't all of you have “measles” that are better to get than not get?

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:28.950
In psychological terms, there's plenty of other things other than just breaking out in measles!

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.350
Like what?

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:32.090
For example.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.010
Someone who hasn't played games up until now.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.940
Hey, this is pretty fun!

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:40.410
If they start as an adult and suddenly discover how fun they are,

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.500
they'll get completely absorbed and won't be able to focus at work!

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.780
My dad's like that!

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.960
He never used to play games, but once he picked up a DS, he started having too much fun with it.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:53.080
And now, every free second he gets, he goes bleep-boop like he's in a nightmare!

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:57.820
Yes, the “measles” you get as an adult are pretty bad.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:57.980
Planning rejected just before presentation

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:58.150
Scenario changed day-of

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:58.320
Storyboarding: one year

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:58.480
Storyboards done day of ADR

00:03:58.480 --> 00:03:58.650
Dubbing the day before broadcast

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:58.920
Delivered just in time for broadcast

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.560
Tomoya!  Grab that ball for—

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.460
He's got some “measles”!

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.330
What the hell is this supposed to be!?

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:15.230
Suddenly becoming obsessed with moe anime after becoming an adult makes a fatal wound.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.250
Leaving things up to your economic strength,

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.860
buying all the goods you can whether they're good or bad...

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.740
It'll bankrupt your lifestyle!

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.080
What's up with those?

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.450
She borrowed them from Manseibashi.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.400
Things that don't hurt you very much when you're young

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.190
can become fatal if you contract them as an adult!

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:41.690
Those who focus on sports and don't get used to women become infatuated with women after they get recruited into the pros.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:44.530
They don't practice and their life as an athlete is cut off! {note: 前園真聖}

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:48.890
Even if you think idols are pointless as a boy,

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:52.800
you'll learn how fun He-bleep Project's concerts are when you become an adult,

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.140
blow all your money on their goods,

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.190
and follow them around on tour in a happi coat!

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.200
If you don't eat canned corned beef,

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.510
you'll taste it for the first time as an adult,

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:02.760
realize how delicious it is,

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:06.020
and clog your arteries eating nothing but it!

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.570
I'm in despair!

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.770
The dreadfulness of late-onset measles has left me in despair!

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:17.040
What's needed is an antibody.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.160
Negative education.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.620
Otonashi?

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.370
You want me to follow you?

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:29.320
It's super-moving!

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:32.190
What kind of story is it?

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.330
I can't stop myself from crying!

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:40.120
Because someone's dying!

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:44.270
So... How are they dying?

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.370
They're dying of a disease!

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:51.030
I've never read such a sad story!

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.600
When people who haven't really read books

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:58.520
grow up and read a phone novel, they call it “super-moving”...

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.040
It's sad.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:04.030
Those kinds of stories are like that too.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:08.110
Once they start selling, their creators lose their inspiration.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.470
You were there?

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.800
Yes, always.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.450
Misdeeds are like that too.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:17.600
If you're scolded fiercely when you're little and decide not to do it again, it's forgivable,

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:21.060
but as an adult, you'll get arrested right away!

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:24.190
Touching teacher's chest!

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.830
Flipping up skirts!

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.500
Peeking in the bath!

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:28.670
So?

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:31.510
If you don't get your boobie-poking out of the way now, Majiru,

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:34.190
you'll get arrested for it as an adult.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:39.400
Will I be executed!?

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.450
Plenty of people have been slaughtered in society for it.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.950
Slaughtered!?

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.540
I'll do it.  I'll do it!

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.410
But... How?

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:50.470
Amateurs should start with small chests.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.860
Like this?

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.600
It's not good.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.650
Touching breasts isn't good.

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:16.710
Touching breasts isn't good.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.710
Looks like he got a good scolding.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.530
Touching breasts isn't good.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.520
But more for something else than for touching.

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:23.210
Looks like it was good medicine for you, Majiru.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:28.030
I think you've learned not to recklessly touch breasts when you grow up.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.830
I'm depressed.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.080
I want to die.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.580
Oh, I want to die.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.700
Saying you want to die when you're young is like measles.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:40.890
If you grow up and do it like Teacher,

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.740
you'll become that guy who makes everyone around you break out in laughter.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.090
Break out in laughter!?

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:48.940
No way!  I don't want to end up like him!

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.020
Are you really that far off, Majiru?

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:55.040
Then you've gotta try wanting to die.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.020
Welp, guess I should die.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:05.390
This is a kind of measles it's okay not to have.

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:06.810
Then don't give it to me!

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:09.000
Beyond that,

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.790
it's better to try lightly immoral business practices as a kid!

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:14.860
One more time!

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.000
Locchi!

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:20.780
If you try them when you grow up, it'll be too late.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:24.050
Does anyone want to buy some detergent?

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:25.580
Anyway,

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:28.690
late-onset measles are troublesome!

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:33.690
Teacher.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:36.820
Who are you?

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.430
I'm a freshman from the next school over.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:51.050
You've gotten popular, teacher.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.460
W-What are you saying!?

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:59.220
Isn't female students falling for their teacher a kind of measles?

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.190
Measles!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.590
If we don't get them...

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:11.430
Measles!  Measles!

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:16.670
Teacher, I've found a way to get out of coming to school legally!

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:19.920
Also, to deceive more female students!

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.070
Whisper whisper.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.640
I see!

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.950
Oh my.  This class is pretty quiet.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:37.190
Class is canceled. Due to measles.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:44.370
I don't think this solves the root of the problem.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:49.280
It's the other way around. If someone who's gonna become a teacher isn't immunized,

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:52.340
he'll go for the female students when he becomes one!

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.010
I caught the real thing...

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:03.720
It's better to play meat doll when you're little.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:07.680
If you do it once you've grown up, your friends will be bigger too,

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:10.490
and you'll need lots of kite string and raw meat.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:14.640
And if the neighbors see you, the effect will likely be lost.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:16.010
What the hell are you playing!?

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:19.370
How to play meat doll!

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:23.100
First, cover a friend in meat!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.360
Next, tie them with kite string!

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.740
Leave them in the sun for three days!

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:34.490
When they're done, beat the pigeons away and play!

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:56.830
Oh, this is

00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.840
Oora's house.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.380
Is this the political party Oora supports?

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:08.210
It sure seems that way.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:17.060
Hi!

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:19.890
Mind if I post this?

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:20.960
Sure!

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:23.960
It's fine, go right ahead!

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:26.310
Can I post this?

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:27.800
Go ahead.

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:38.110
Seems like it's just an open-hearted, magnanimous household.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:43.180
So... I was thinking,

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.890
why not increase the number of points? {corners/vectors}

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:46.050
Net

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:46.220
Blog

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:46.380
Game

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:46.550
Comic

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:46.720
Novel

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:46.990
Anime

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:53.490
Why not increase the number of points? {corners/vectors}

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.990
If there aren't enough points, things get prickly! {punning on kado point/kado ga tatsu become aggravated}

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:59.760
With just you and one other point, a sharp, piercing spear is formed.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.570
By adding more points, it becomes smooth,

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:04.140
unpiercing, unprickly.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:08.010
For example, by only placing posters for one party, things become noisy.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:11.680
But by putting up plenty of them, you're simply thought of as an open-hearted person.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:12.980
Even for cults!

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:16.750
If there's just one, things get prickly,

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.720
but if there's plenty, no one worries!

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:23.390
People think each one isn't -too- bad.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:26.470
If you have a complex about one thing, it'll be attacked.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.390
Baldy!

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:30.600
But if you have four or five, no one will say anything!

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.230
If you were wearing clothes, you'd just be a trespasser.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:36.960
But if you're naked, it's too easy to crack jokes and no one gets angry!

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:46.410
Oh no!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:49.410
Meru's abusive language has pierced Teacher!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:52.040
It's just one insult, so it's piercing.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.520
If there were five or six, it wouldn't be prickly.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:58.770
This is horrible in and of itself!

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:01.810
But each individual word hurts less.

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:06.280
Really, in some country somewhere, there are far more insulting words than there are in Japanese.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:10.800
Since you're insulted even as a greeting, none of them really matter.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:12.620
I see.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:17.830
By adding points, society won't loathe me anymore.

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:19.230
Like this!

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.920
No, that's only one point.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:28.020
I thought I put in plenty of variations!

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.120
From society's viewpoint, it's all the same.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.270
Well, I guess if people don't realize it's no good.

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.930
It's something where you tried to add points, but ended up with only one!

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:40.030
That's right, it was a great loss!

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:44.640
Even though they were promoted as diversified investments to spread risk!

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:48.000
The entire world has been routed due to the panic!

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:49.710
Ultimately, the investments were a single point!

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:52.820
How many times are they going to have to stop the Chuo line today!?

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:54.080
Well, let's leave discussions which are too realistic behind for now.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:57.330
Nutrition is like that too.

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:00.250
I put my heart into keeping a balance.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.850
No, that's completely off-center.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:04.160
Anyway.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.790
Things become less prickly when you add points!

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:10.500
Love triangles are like that too.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:12.730
If there's three points, things are prickly.

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:15.280
That may very well be true.

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.470
Like this, the points quickly become piercing.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:21.470
But like this, it's a bit smoother.

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.070
The “Cats Card” has four points!

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.050
But even with four points it's still prickly!

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:34.530
To smooth over the prickliness, we need more and more points!

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:37.340
Otherwise the class will become bloodthirsty!

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:39.390
Really!?

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:44.760
I'm sorry!

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:46.700
I'm sorry!  I'm sorry!

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:48.430
More and more points!

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:49.430
Sixth point!

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:50.440
Seventh point!

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:51.430
Eighth point!

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:52.450
Ninth point!

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.440
Tenth point!

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:54.540
Eleventh point!

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.660
Twelfth point!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:56.760
Thirteenth point!

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:57.990
Fourteenth point!

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:00.040
By adding more and more points,

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.300
the polygon will become infinitely close to being a circle,

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:03.580
and mankind will be at peace!

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:05.320
Chiri, you too!

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:10.080
You're unusually cheerful.

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:11.710
Really.

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.810
No damn way.

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:17.700
Adding more women makes things less prickly?

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.570
The hell are you, Ishida Jun'ichi!?

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:20.730
I knew it!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.230
The hell are you, Morimoto Leo!?

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:26.200
Looks like the points are still pointy.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:29.910
You still don't have enough relationships with different women!

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:32.290
Isn't it strange?

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:36.880
By adding more points, will I be freed from this unspeakable horror?

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:39.890
Get more relationships with people in town!

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:59.680
How many are you up to now?

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:02.310
I'm in about a 53-way relationship!

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.580
It's almost a circle!

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.840
Soon, the world will be at peace!

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:21.730
Are you a fool?

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:27.330
The more women you get, the heavier your sins become.

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.300
With this kind of circle—!

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.980
Teacher, your theory was refuted!

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:35.840
It was half yours, wasn't it!?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:39.630
If I just use my spade, it'll be prickly,

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:41.210
so to be milder,

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.970
I've added points.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:49.890
That's just one point!

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:52.050
I'll borrow one.

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:53.490
Me too.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:04.670
Sorry I'm late.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:09.870
All right.

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:17.730
Isn't she concerned about this?

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:19.920
She's a magnanimous girl.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:22.620
Anyway, I keep picturing all these little kids playing some game in this big field of rye and all.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:22.790
Thousands of little kids kids, and nobody's around - nobody big, I mean - except me.

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:22.950
And I'm standing on the edge of some crazy cliff.

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:23.120
What I have to do, I have 
to catch everybody if they 
start to go over the cliff 
- I mean if they're running 
and they don't look where 
they're going I have to 
come out from somewhere 
and catch them.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:23.290
That's all I do all day. I'd just be the catcher in the rye and all.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:23.550
I know it's crazy, but that's the only thing I'd really like to be.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.460
Oh, teacher.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.060
Through life?

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:37.200
It's a kind lifestyle where you ignore many things.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:41.570
Didn't we use this same kind of gag a long time ago?

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.570
Ignore that too.

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:47.090
Teacher, it looks like you finally get through life!

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:49.220
You mean like what we just did?

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:54.120
It's not that bad. I think I'll try it out.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.960
Ignoring that.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.600
Definitely ignoring that.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:06.830
Ignoring that.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:07.800
Ignoring that.

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:08.630
Ignoring that.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:09.430
Ignoring that.

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:10.270
Ignoring that.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.500
I'm ignoring them all!

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:17.920
If you put it that way, I'm experiencing through life too.

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:19.090
Ohkusa?

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:24.380
Even though I know it, I ignore when my husband's horny.

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:28.690
I don't have the money to go to hospital, so I ignore pains.

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:32.790
I ignore N-bleep-K's demands for money.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.880
If I don't ignore them, I wouldn't be able to go on with my daily life!

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:40.160
I don't know how to put this, but I'm sorry for ignoring things as a hobby.

00:18:52.010 --> 00:18:54.610
Why don't you just ignore that?

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:57.670
A hit-and-run!?

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:02.520
No way.  There's no way a hit-and-run would happen right in front of us.

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:05.390
He's just ignoring things that happen while driving.

00:19:05.390 --> 00:19:07.190
You could call it a “drive through”.

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:09.960
Are you trying to be clever!?

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:14.800
Teacher!  Chiri's starting to thoroughly place “made by” labels!

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:18.140
What's this!?

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:20.150
It's a “made by” label.

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:23.640
Nowadays, it's normal to be able to see who grew your veggies!

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:27.910
Let's make it so you can see the faces of the people who made everything!

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:30.750
Knock it off!  You'll crush dreams!

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.320
No!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.390
Oh, hey, Chiri.

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:46.960
Who made -you-?

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.020
This is too horrible!

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:55.830
It's like the faux pas a middle-schooler would make.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:02.150
All right, I'll make it so you can see the faces of the people who made everything!

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:04.710
There!

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:06.300
There!

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:07.750
There!

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:13.990
Umm... On this picture of my parents, you got my dad wrong...

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:16.490
The one who made you doesn't care.

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:18.000
What!?

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:19.960
You're wrong, Chiri.

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:22.470
All people are children of God!

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.220
Are you on about Balbora the Third again!?

00:20:25.220 --> 00:20:27.670
That's who made you.

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:30.410
Since Japan is the land of myriad gods,

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:33.410
each person was made by a different god.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:36.810
Is this my Creator?

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:39.020
Who!?

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:43.520
Those are god stickers that came with chocolate bars.

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:48.250
Brother, the manufacturing line is in full operation!

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:50.500
It's like it prints money!

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:55.170
Doesn't this mean we're accomplices in selling trinkets?

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:03.220
There's a total of 81!

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:06.410
Gotta catch 'em all!

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:44.590
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:46.940
Matching the song, let's draw with a G-pen, okay?

00:22:48.390 --> 00:22:54.830
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:22:54.830 --> 00:23:01.260
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:02.780
Lightning...

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:04.500
Flash!

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:06.060
Lightning...

00:23:06.060 --> 00:23:07.750
Flash!

00:23:07.750 --> 00:23:10.830
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:14.180
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:14.180 --> 00:23:16.970
Two puddles were made.

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:20.540
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:24.950
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:24.950 --> 00:23:28.670
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:28.670 --> 00:23:31.330
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:33.490
Bye bye!
